# .agent/projects.local — per-machine project registry (issue #227, #172 step 2;
# parent roots and trailing fields: issue #265)
#
# Copy this file to .agent/projects.local (gitignored). The registry is the
# only link between the workspace and the projects it serves; a project may
# live anywhere on disk.
#
# One project per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <name>  <project_type>  [<path>]  [key=value ...]
#
#   name          Project identity on this machine. Also the worktree repo
#                 key and (for now) the default hosting dir projects/<name>.
#                 Allowed: [A-Za-z0-9._-], must start with a letter or
#                 digit; '..' is not allowed.
#   project_type  Adapter type; must exist at .agent/project_types/<type>/
#                 (ADR-0011). Currently: single_project, ros2_colcon.
#                 The pseudo-type "project" declares a PARENT ROOT: a
#                 directory that groups several instances of one project
#                 (e.g. one per ROS distro). It has no adapter and need not
#                 be a git repository; it is the session and memory unit.
#   path          Optional hosting directory (absolute, or relative to the
#                 workspace root; default projects/<name>). No spaces or
#                 "=" (a third token containing "=" is read as a field).
#   key=value     Optional trailing fields (no spaces in values):
#                   parent=<name>            this line is an instance of
#                                            parent root <name>
#                   worktrees=<path>         where this root's worktrees
#                                            live (default <path>/worktrees)
#                   role=<name>              passed to the adapter as
#                                            ACTIVE_PROJECT_ROLE
#                   distro=<name>            passed to the adapter as
#                                            ACTIVE_PROJECT_DISTRO; for
#                                            ros2_colcon this is the ROS
#                                            distro (overrides ROS_DISTRO in
#                                            projects.d/<name>.sh; must agree
#                                            with the manifest if that names
#                                            one)
#                   default_instance=<name>  parent lines only: the instance
#                                            used when the parent is
#                                            selected without --project
#
# single_project checkouts are managed manually: clone the project into
# its hosting dir, then register it here. ros2_colcon instances bootstrap
# themselves from an empty hosting dir — register the name, set its
# bootstrap_url (below) to the project's bootstrap.yaml, and run
# `.agent/scripts/adapter --project <name> setup` (or `make build
# PROJECT=<name>` after setup).
#
# Per-project settings (issue #332) go in .agent/projects.d/<name> (no
# extension; gitignored, per machine), one key=value per line, written with
# `.agent/scripts/project_setting.sh set <name> key=value ...` or by hand:
#
#   # .agent/projects.d/boat_sim
#   build=./scripts/build.sh
#   test=make test
#   install=none
#   instructions=none
#
#   build, test, install  a command run from the project root, split on
#                         blanks and run without a shell (no quotes, & | ;
#                         < > $ ( ) ` or backslash: anything needing them is
#                         a script, so point the key at one), or 'none' for
#                         a recorded "this project has none". ros2_colcon
#                         reads install only: colcon owns its build and
#                         tests, so build and test are refused for it
#   bootstrap_url         ros2_colcon only: http(s):// or file:// URL of the
#                         project's bootstrap.yaml (refused for
#                         single_project, which is cloned by hand)
#
# A key the project's type never reads is refused by `set`, and a
# hand-written one fails `check` and stops the adapter; each type lists
# such keys in .agent/project_types/<type>/unused_settings.
#   location              project | outside       where the loop's work
#   location_path         absolute path           plans and progress
#   tracking              project | untracked | repo   timelines live
#   instructions          none | tracked  (may the workspace offer agent
#                         instructions in tracked project files)
#
# Lines starting with '#' are comments (no trailing comments: a command may
# contain '#'). An unknown or duplicate key or an empty value is an error,
# and a malformed file stops every adapter verb for the project.
#
# Records settings: valid combinations are (project, project), (project,
# untracked), (outside, untracked) and (outside, repo); a records repository
# must not be a workspace. With neither key set a project's records are
# (project, project): committed in the project on the issue's feature
# branch, as today. That default, the zero-footprint proposal and the
# default outside layout are PROVISIONAL (project_records_default in
# _project_registry.sh). Only (project, project) is honoured until the
# records lookup lands (#393); project_setting.sh refuses to store another.
#
# Precedence for build/test/install/bootstrap_url: the settings file, key by
# key; for a key it does not set, the LEGACY .agent/projects.d/<name>.sh (a
# sourced shell file: BUILD_CMD, TEST_CMD, INSTALL_CMD,
# MANIFEST_BOOTSTRAP_URL, and variables such as ROS_DISTRO and ROS_ROOT_DIR,
# which stay there) when that file exists, otherwise the shared
# .agent/project_config.sh. The legacy file, when present, is the whole
# legacy layer, as before #332: the shared file is not consulted for a
# variable it leaves unset (a legacy file with only BUILD_CMD gets no shared
# TEST_CMD). A registered project that falls through to the shared file gets
# a note on stderr. A legacy ros2_colcon config looks like:
#
#   # .agent/projects.d/shore_tools-jazzy.sh
#   MANIFEST_BOOTSTRAP_URL="https://<host>/<manifest-repo>/raw/jazzy/config/bootstrap.yaml"
#
# A project name may not end in ".sh" (its settings file would collide with
# another project's legacy file).
#
# One instance per distro: a second distro of the same project is a second
# registry entry with its OWN hosting dir. Group them under a parent root
# so sessions, memory and instructions have one home. Never point two
# entries at one dir — setup reuses an existing manifest checkout with only
# a warning on a branch mismatch, so the second instance would silently
# read the first one's manifest.
#
# How the active project is resolved (adapter dispatcher):
#   1. --project <name> (or: make build PROJECT=<name>)
#   2. current directory inside a registered hosting dir (longest match, so
#      a cwd inside an instance resolves to the instance, not its parent)
#   3. legacy project/ symlink (unchanged behavior)
#   A parent root selected by 1 or 2 resolves to its default_instance, else
#   its only instance; several instances without a default is an error
#   that lists them.
#
# Examples:
#boat_sim            single_project  /home/me/src/boat_sim
#coastal             single_project  /data/checkouts/coastal_mapper
#shore_tools         project         /home/me/shore_tools          default_instance=shore_tools-rolling
#shore_tools-jazzy   ros2_colcon     /home/me/shore_tools/jazzy    parent=shore_tools distro=jazzy   role=dev
#shore_tools-rolling ros2_colcon     /home/me/shore_tools/rolling  parent=shore_tools distro=rolling role=dev
